bp 640w, /assets/img/photos/red-barn-snow.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width:700px) 100vw, (max-width:1020px) 50vw, 33vw" width="1200" height="900" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></a><div class="in"><span class="meta">Franklin County</span><h2><a href="/vermont-towns/st-albans/">St. Albans</a></h2><p>Franklin County’s seat sits above St. Albans Bay near the Canadian border, with a Victorian downtown around…</p><a class="more" href="/vermont-towns/st-albans/" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true">Local page →</a></div></article><article class="card rv town-card"><a class="ph" href="/vermont-towns/brattleboro/" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/assets/img/photos/fallen-trees-building.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/fallen-trees-building-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/fallen-trees-building.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width:700px) 100vw, (max-width:1020px) 50vw, 33vw" width="1200" height="900" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></a><div class="in"><span class="meta">Windham County</span><h2><a href="/vermont-towns/brattleboro/">Brattleboro</a></h2><p>Brattleboro climbs the hills above the big river on Vermont’s eastern border, where Whetstone Brook runs…</p><a class="more" href="/vermont-towns/brattleboro/" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true">Local page →</a></div></article><article class="card rv town-card"><a class="ph" href="/vermont-towns/bennington/" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/assets/img/photos/bennington-aerial.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/bennington-aerial-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/bennington-aerial.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width:700px) 100vw, (max-width:1020px) 50vw, 33vw" width="1200" height="900" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></a><div class="in"><span class="meta">Bennington County</span><h2><a href="/vermont-towns/bennington/">Bennington</a></h2><p>Bennington spreads along the Walloomsac River below Mount Anthony, with Old Bennington’s historic homes on…</p><a class="more" href="/vermont-towns/bennington/" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true">Local page →</a></div></article><article class="card rv town-card"><a class="ph" href="/vermont-towns/middlebury/" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/assets/img/photos/barn-roof-crew.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/barn-roof-crew-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/barn-roof-crew.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width:700px) 100vw, (max-width:1020px) 50vw, 33vw" width="1200" height="900" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></a><div class="in"><span class="meta">Addison County</span><h2><a href="/vermont-towns/middlebury/">Middlebury</a></h2><p>Addison County’s shire town straddles Otter Creek Falls, with a college, a historic village center and open…</p><a class="more" href="/vermont-towns/middlebury/" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true">Local page →</a></div></article><article class="card rv town-card"><a class="ph" href="/vermont-towns/st-johnsbury/" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/assets/img/photos/fairbanks-museum.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/fairbanks-museum-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/fairbanks-museum.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width:700px) 100vw, (max-width:1020px) 50vw, 33vw" width="1200" height="900" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></a><div class="in"><span class="meta">Caledonia County</span><h2><a href="/vermont-towns/st-johnsbury/">St. Johnsbury</a></h2><p>The hub of the Northeast Kingdom sits where the Passumpsic, Moose and Sleepers rivers meet, with a Victorian…</p><a class="more" href="/vermont-towns/st-johnsbury/" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true">Local page →</a></div></article><article class="card rv town-card"><a class="ph" href="/vermont-towns/stowe/" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/assets/img/photos/snow-roof-eaves.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/snow-roof-eaves-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/snow-roof-eaves.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width:700px) 100vw, (max-width:1020px) 50vw, 33vw" width="1200" height="1210" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></a><div class="in"><span class="meta">Lamoille County</span><h2><a href="/vermont-towns/stowe/">Stowe</a></h2><p>Stowe sits below Mount Mansfield, Vermont’s highest peak, where lodges, condos and high-end second homes…</p><a class="more" href="/vermont-towns/stowe/" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true">Local page →</a></div></article><article class="card rv town-card"><a class="ph" href="/vermont-towns/hartford/" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/assets/img/photos/covered-bridge.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/covered-bridge-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/covered-bridge.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width:700px) 100vw, (max-width:1020px) 50vw, 33vw" width="1200" height="836" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></a><div class="in"><span class="meta">Windsor County</span><h2><a href="/vermont-towns/hartford/">Hartford</a></h2><p>Hartford’s villages, including White River Junction, Quechee and Wilder, sit where the White River meets the…</p><a class="more" href="/vermont-towns/hartford/" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true">Local page →</a></div></article></div></div></section>
<section class="sec mist"><div class="wrap"><div class="sec-head rv"><span class="kicker">Regions</span><h2>How claims differ around Vermont</h2><p>The same policy language plays out differently in a Burlington triplex, a Stowe ski condo and a Northeast Kingdom farmhouse.</p></div><div class="regions" data-stagger><article class="region rv"><div class="ph"><img src="/assets/img/photos/red-barn-snow.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/red-barn-snow-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/red-barn-snow.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width:700px) 100vw, 25vw" width="1200" height="900" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></div><div class="in"><h3>Champlain Valley &amp; the northwest</h3><p>Vermont’s most populated region mixes dense older neighborhoods, condos, lake camps and dairy farms. Wind off the lake, ice storms and summer hail are the main weather risks.</p><p class="towns">Burlington, South Burlington, St. Albans, Middlebury</p></div></article><article class="region rv"><div class="ph"><img src="/assets/img/photos/foliage-ridge.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/foliage-ridge-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/foliage-ridge.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width:700px) 100vw, 25vw" width="1200" height="800" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></div><div class="in"><h3>Central Vermont &amp; the Green Mountains</h3><p>River towns that flooded in 2023 and 2024, plus ski-country homes and condos carrying some of the heaviest snow loads in the state.</p><p class="towns">Montpelier, Barre, Stowe, Waterbury</p></div></article><article class="region rv"><div class="ph"><img src="/assets/img/photos/fairbanks-museum.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/fairbanks-museum-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/fairbanks-museum.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width:700px) 100vw, 25vw" width="1200" height="900" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></div><div class="in"><h3>The Northeast Kingdom</h3><p>Long cold winters, remote properties and wood heat. Freeze-ups, snow load and chimney fires lead the claim list, and repair costs reflect the distance.</p><p class="towns">St. Johnsbury, Lyndon, Newport, Island Pond</p></div></article><article class="region rv"><div class="ph"><img src="/assets/img/photos/bennington-aerial.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/bennington-aerial-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/bennington-aerial.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width:700px) 100vw, 25vw" width="1200" height="900" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></div><div class="in"><h3>Southern Vermont &amp; the eastern river valleys</h3><p>Irene hit this region hardest in 2011. Historic village homes, hillside lots and river valleys shape both the losses and the repair costs.</p><p class="towns">Brattleboro, Bennington, Rutland, Hartford</p></div></article></div></div></section>
